    "q-210510": {
      "dom_id": "step-q210510",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Insert the missing number in the multiplication problem below.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n\n<table align=\"center\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n</td>\n<td>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"3\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$\\times $</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$=$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n</td>\n<td>\n\n<table align=\"center\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{4}{6}$ on the left and $\\frac{4}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/54e0c1ae73fdf546507c8a4f486f911f1ef8f6bfb57da249a1654393a63151b4.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $4$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $4$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{4}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
