      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/ead50e432af5a01d8c04109698a5543547225d149c979f694e54208231946710.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?",
      "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{3}{5}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{4}$, we split the whole into $4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/9c885c7cb5ee0cd3ac9f9166e41b3455732a99a574f18b147602f6109416610e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{3}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/503598e9174ef0276190165b397e5e9d69972e0df9ac6e83a9e4f9258b98fb60.png)",
